# procmon-check filter (conceptual template)
#
# Placeholder — programmatic filtering via the CSV-level post-filter in
# `csv_check.rs` is currently the authoritative gate. ProcMon's `.pmc`
# configuration file is a binary container (the GUI saves it via
# File → Save Filter), so we ship this plain-text template as a
# documentation artifact rather than a real `.pmc` file.
#
# If a future maintainer wants ProcMon to do the filtering server-side
# (performance — reduces .pml size on long traces), generate a real
# `.pmc` via ProcMon UI and place it here, then update `procmon.rs` to
# pass `/LoadConfig <this file>` to the capture invocation.
#
# Conceptual filter the post-filter currently enforces:
#
#   INCLUDE
#     Process Name == trackly.exe
#     Operation == WriteFile
#       OR Operation == CreateFile
#       OR Operation == SetEndOfFileInformationFile
#       OR Operation == WriteFileGather
#       OR Operation == SetAllocationInformationFile
#       OR Operation == SetBasicInformationFile
#
#   EXCLUDE (overrides include)
#     <none — all matching rows are evaluated by csv_check.rs>
#
# Forbidden path fragments (case-insensitive, slash-insensitive — applied
# in csv_check::normalize):
#   - \AppData\Local\
#   - \AppData\Roaming\
#   - \AppData\LocalLow\
#   - \ProgramData\
#
# Allowed prefixes (case-insensitive, slash-insensitive):
#   - <sandbox path>  (e.g. %TEMP%\trackly_procmon_<uuid>\Документы\Учёт\Trackly\)
#   - %TEMP%          (sandbox lives here; transient temp files are accepted)
